  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 400°F. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, peel, and trim carrots; halve lengthwise. Transfer carrots to a large baking sheet pan, then drizzle with oil and season with spices. Toss to combine and spread out in an even layer.  \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "3 tbsp extra virgin olive oil\n½ tsp garlic powder\n½ tsp salt\n¼ tsp black pepper\n⅛ tsp cayenne pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place baking sheet in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and roast, turning halfway through, until carrots are golden brown and fork-tender, 20-25 minutes. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Meanwhile, preheat a skillet over medium heat. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Once the skillet is hot, add hazelnuts, pine nuts, sesame seeds, coriander seeds, and cumin seeds; toast, stirring frequently, until golden and fragrant, 2-3 minutes. Remove from heat and let cool, 5 minutes. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "3 tbsp hazelnuts, chopped\n2 tbsp pine nuts\n½ tbsp sesame seeds\n1 tsp coriander seeds\n1 tsp cumin seeds"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Transfer toasted nuts and seeds to a food processor. Add spices, then pulse several times until nuts are finely chopped and dukkah is combined.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "¼ tsp paprika\n¼ tsp oregano, dried\n⅛ tsp salt\n⅛ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "When the carrots are done, remove from the oven. Transfer to a serving platter and sprinkle with the dukkah. Enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
